FINAL ANSWER:
Yes, it is basically one person. Andrew Gallant holds about three quarters of the surviving Rust lines.

**Scope:** 9 `.rs` files at HEAD, 3,303 non-blank lines attributed (3,719 with blank lines). Counting uses `git blame -w -M -C`, with commit counts from 191 non-merge commits.

| Author | Lines | Share | Commits | Share |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Andrew Gallant | 2,489 | 75.4% | 128 | 67.0% |
| Inès Moreau (3 addresses) | 189 | 5.7% | 3 | 1.6% |
| Sebastian Thiel | 66 | 2.0% | 1 | 0.5% |
| Ashley | 65 | 2.0% | 2 | 1.0% |
| Aron Griffis | 56 | 1.7% | 1 | 0.5% |
| Niv Kaminer | 43 | 1.3% | 2 | 1.0% |
| mcharsley | 43 | 1.3% | 1 | 0.5% |
| Marvin Löbel | 39 | 1.2% | 1 | 0.5% |
| Martin Sehnoutka | 38 | 1.2% | 1 | 0.5% |
| Yufeng Wang | 36 | 1.1% | 3 | 1.6% |

31 more authors hold 7.2% together. The largest of them is Garrett Berg at 1.0%.

**Bus factor:** this is the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines reach 50% of the lines counted, computed over all the `.rs` files. It is 1, because Gallant alone holds 75.4%. Reaching 80% takes 2 authors. Only Gallant is above 6%. Nobody else holds more than 5.7%.

**What the figures leave out or assume:**
- **Dropped file:** `src/ucd_tables.rs` (647 lines) is generated, so it is left out of every number.
- **Bot:** `github-actions[bot]` (9 lines, 1 commit) is excluded and gets no credit.
- **Merged identities (a guess from names and addresses, nothing written to `.mailmap`):**
  - Inès Moreau is three addresses counted as one person: 105 lines from `ines@moreau.example`, 84 from `ines.moreau@university.example`, and 0 from a noreply address. Unmerged, the largest address holds 105 lines, about 3.2%.
  - Igor Gnatenko is also merged, but holds 0 surviving lines, so the table does not show them.
- **Same address, several names:** Niv Kaminer also appears as `nivkner` (43 lines), and Alisha Aneja also appears as `Alisha` (9 lines). Both are counted as one person.
- **Possible same person, not merged:** Ashley (65 lines) and Ashley Mannix (4 lines) share a name, but the evidence is weak. I led with them separate. Merged, they would be 69 lines (2.1%). Only you can confirm that.
- **Rustfmt commit:** the tool flagged `c584a1d` ("style: switch to rustfmt", Gallant, 2020-01-11) as probably mechanical but did not set it aside. It touched 9 files, including `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and `rustfmt.toml`. The `--ignore-rev` re-run leaves Gallant at 2,481 lines (75.1%) against 2,489 (75.4%), so it doesn't change the picture. The tool also reported 0 mechanical rewrites set aside among the 77 commits it examined. That check covered all of them, not a sample.
- **Copy detection (`-C`):** moving or copying code between files shifted 146 lines to other authors. Without copy detection Gallant would hold 2,635 lines (79.8%). With it he holds 2,489 (75.4%). Ashley goes from 36 lines (1.1%) to 65 (2.0%), and Garrett Berg from 0 to 33.

**Limits:** these numbers show whose lines survive, not code quality, review work, design work, or code that was deleted on purpose.
